# Project Stack
#
# Generated by bootstrap.py — edit values below to match your project.
# This file is read by all SDD_Pro agents at every invocation.
# `workspace/input/stack/stack.md` is gitignored (contains local secrets
# via env vars) ; this `.template` file is the versioned skeleton.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ⚠️ SECURITY — ENV VARS ONLY (v7.0.0 hardening, 2026-05-21)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NEVER hardcode secrets in this file. Sections `## Active Auth Specs`,
# `## Active Database`, `## Active SMTP Server` declare only the NAMES of
# environment variables to read at runtime. Values are resolved by :
#   - .NET    : `Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("DB_PASSWORD")` or
#               `builder.Configuration["DB_PASSWORD"]` (auto env binding).
#   - Spring  : `@Value("${DB_PASSWORD}")` + `spring-dotenv` for local .env.
#   - Node    : `process.env.DB_PASSWORD` (load `.env` via `dotenv`).
#   - Python  : `os.environ["DB_PASSWORD"]` (load `.env` via `python-dotenv`).
#
# Convention SDD_Pro v7.0.0 : `KEY: ${KEY}` means "agent reads env var
# named KEY". A hardcoded value in these sections is a bug to fix.
# Dev machine setup : set vars via `setx VAR value` (Windows) or
# `export VAR=value` (Unix), OR project-level `.env` file (gitignored).
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

## Project Config
# FrontendName/BackendName = project names ; AppNamespace/BackendNamespace
# auto-derived (= project name, cf. CLAUDE.md §1 + ownership.md §1.bis).
# For fullstack stacks : drop the "Front" suffix (e.g. {{AppName}}Front → {{AppName}}).
AppName: {{AppName}}
FrontendName: {{AppName}}
FrontendLocalPort: {{FrontendPort}}
BackendName: {{BackendName}}
BackendLocalPort: {{BackendPort}}
LibStrategy: {{LibStrategy}}
PlanReviewDefault: true

# QA mode :
#   off | quality-only | tests-only | tests+coverage | full | manual
QAMode: tests+coverage
CoverageMin: 80
MaxParallel: 3

# Cost caps (USD, see config.base.yml for full doc) :
MaxCostPerRun: 50
BuildLoopMaxCostUsd: 15
BuildLoopMaxIter: 3

# FailOn severity thresholds : info | minor | moderate | serious | critical
CodeReviewFailOn: critical
SecurityFailOn: critical
SpecComplianceFailOn: serious
ArchReviewFailOn: serious

# US granularity (1-6 per FEAT recommended) :
UsGranularityTarget: 3

# OWASP scan : keep true for serious runs
SecurityScanEnabled: true

# Auditor modes : off | manual | full
CodeReviewMode: full
SecurityMode: full
SpecComplianceMode: full
ArchReviewMode: manual
A11yMode: "off"
PerfMode: "off"

